From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 02:42:10 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 108/110] Meridian: an AAC track FFmpeg didn't decode is float
 planar

FFmpeg has no AAC decoder in Meridian to fill in its sample format, so
an AAC track would be dropped as invalid; macOS decodes it to float
planar, as AC3 gets S16 here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
---
 media/ffmpeg/ffmpeg_common.cc | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/media/ffmpeg/ffmpeg_common.cc b/media/ffmpeg/ffmpeg_common.cc
index e4c443001d..591d20e75e 100644
--- a/media/ffmpeg/ffmpeg_common.cc
+++ b/media/ffmpeg/ffmpeg_common.cc
@@ -403,6 +403,12 @@ bool AVCodecContextToAudioDecoderConfig(const AVCodecContext* codec_context,
 #else
       NOTREACHED();
 #endif
+    // Meridian: nor for AAC, which macOS decodes (AudioToolbox, float planar).
+    case AudioCodec::kAAC:
+      if (sample_format == kUnknownSampleFormat) {
+        sample_format = kSampleFormatPlanarF32;
+      }
+      break;
 #if BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_PLATFORM_MPEG_H_AUDIO)
     case AudioCodec::kMpegHAudio:
       channel_layout = CHANNEL_LAYOUT_BITSTREAM;
